# MC Compliance Gate — local-inference

Fleet-hard repo (`petralabx/local-inference`, tier tooling). Canonical SOP:
https://github.com/petralabx/PLX_MC/blob/main/docs/AGENT-PR-SOP.md

## Non-negotiable close-out

```bash
# Mint with this repo's exact slug (Portal/Hub stamps are wrong-scope here)
COMPLIANCE_CAPTURE=1 MC_REPO=petralabx/local-inference \
  MC_BASE_URL=https://mc.plxcustomer.io MC_ACCOUNTABLE=cos@petrasoap.com \
  MC_MCP_API_KEY=… MC_TASK_ID=TASK-NNN \
  node scripts/compliance-checkout.mjs

# After PR open + evidence hand-in — must exit 0 before claiming done
MC_REPO=petralabx/local-inference MC_MCP_API_KEY=… \
  node scripts/compliance-pr-verify.mjs --wait
```

`mc_complete_task` returning ok is **not** gate success (local-inference#11).
Only GitHub `compliance` SUCCESS / verify exit 0 is.

## Order: complete only after the last push

Completing a task closes its checkout, so the stamp stops resolving and any
later push re-runs the gate into `decision 3: checkout handshake required`
(local-inference#13). Keep the checkout open until the branch is final:

    checkout -> PR -> gate green -> merge -> complete

If a push is unavoidable after completing, mint a fresh checkout for the same
task and replace the stamp line in the PR body before the gate re-runs.

Prefer `bash scripts/mc-checkout-local-inference.sh TASK-NNN` when the MCP key
is hydrated from AWS. Never invent stamps; never edit
`.github/workflows/*compliance*`.
